RECSEW



Mount Rainier Recreational Forecast

National Weather Service Seattle WA

400 PM PDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.SYNOPSIS...A cooler weather system will cross Mount Rainier

National Park this evening, spreading showers and perhaps an

isolated thunderstorm as snow levels fall below Camp Muir.  

Cooler and cloudier conditions will linger into Thursday, with 

showers tapering during the day. Warmer and drier conditions will

develop at the park on Friday and persist into early next week as

high pressure returns to the region.



&&



.WEDNESDAY NIGHT...Mostly cloudy. Showers, with a  slight chance 

of thunderstorms in the evening. Snow level near 10500 feet 

decreasing to 8000 feet after midnight.

.THURSDAY...Mostly sunny. A slight chance of showers in the

morning. Snow level near 7500 feet. 

.THURSDAY NIGHT...Partly cloudy. Freezing level near 12000 feet. 

.FRIDAY...Sunny. Freezing level near 13500 feet. 



&&



