085

FNUS75 KMSO 062303

FWSMSO



Spot Forecast for Dominic Point

National Weather Service Missoula MT

503 PM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0600 MDT on August 07. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...Overcast skies with slight chance of showers

increasing overnight into Thursday morning.

Cool temperatures with showers likely and chance for 

thunderstorms Thursday afternoon. Frequent lightning likely and 

small hail possible. 10% chance to get 0.45" or more of 

precipitation and 40+ mph outflow winds from direct impact of 

thunderstorm. Drying and staying cool with partly cloudy skies 

into Friday.



.TONIGHT...



* Sky/Weather.........Mostly cloudy. Slight chance of rain showers

  and thunderstorms in the evening, then slight chance of rain 

  overnight. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...10 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....15 percent. 

* Min Temperature.....48-53. 

* Max Humidity........64-69 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Southwest 4-8 mph with gusts up to 20 mph in

  the evening becoming variable 1-4 mph with gusts up to 10 mph

  overnight.

* Precip Amount.......0.00-0.05 inches. 



.THURSDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Mostly cloudy. Chance of rain showers and

  slight chance of thunderstorms in the morning, then rain showers

  likely and chance of thunderstorms in the afternoon. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...70 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....80 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....58-63. 

* Min Humidity........52-57 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable 1-4 mph with gusts up to 10 mph in

  the morning becoming west-northwest 5-10 mph with gusts to

  around 20 mph in the afternoon and evening. Direct impact from 

  thunderstorm may produce erratic gust to, or in excess of, 40 

  mph.

* Precip Amount.......0.08-0.33 inches. 



.THURSDAY NIGHT...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Rain showers likely and

  chance of thunderstorms in the evening. Slight chance rain

  showers overnight.

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...60 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....35 percent. 

* Min Temperature.....40-45. 

* Max Humidity.......71-76 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........West-northwest 5-10 mph with gusts to around

  20 mph in the evening. Direct impact from thunderstorm may

  produce erratic gust to, or in excess of, 40 mph. Becoming

  variable/southwest 3-8 mph with gusts up to 15 mph overnight.

* Precip Amount.......0.02-0.25 inches. 



.FRIDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Slight chance of rain in the 

  morning. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...Less than 10 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....Up to 10 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....57-62. 

* Min Humidity........39-44 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/southwest 3-8 mph with gusts up to

  15 mph overnight becoming west 6-10 mph with gusts up to 25 mph

  in the afternoon. 

* Precip Amount.......0.00-0.03 inches. 



