FXUS64 KOHX 062305

AFDOHX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Nashville TN

605 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Updated at 602 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



- After several cooler than normal days, temperatures will be near

  normal through the rest of this week, and a little warmer next

  week. Humidity will be tolerable but creeping upward. 



- Low chances for showers and thunderstorms each day, and mainly

  for the Cumberland Plateau. The severe storm threat is very 

  low.



&&



.SHORT TERM...

(Rest of today through Thursday)

Issued at 1112 AM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



This may be a good time to check on the mental well-being of any 

meteorologist in your life, suffering from extreme boredom under 

the current wx pattern. There are no changes and no surprises in

today's forecast. The weak upper trough that has been overhead the

past several days is being nudged out by an expanding ridge 

centered well to our west. This change will end the cooler than 

normal patten we have enjoyed and bring temperatures up to normal 

through the rest of the week. There will be enough moisture and 

instability for a few stray showers or storms each afternoon, 

mainly over the Plateau. No severe wx is expected. There will be 

some patchy fog each night. 



&&



.LONG TERM...

(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)

Issued at 1112 AM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Next week, a new upper level ridge center will develop over 

Florida. This will nudge our temperatures a degree or 2 higher 

and add a little more humidity. Heat index values may reach 100 

in some spots, but at this time we are not expecting any heat 

advisory level conditions. There will be more instability and a 

trough will pass across the Ohio Valley increasing the potential 

for scattered showers and storms across Middle Tennessee (20 to 40

percent each day next week). The added instability may yield a 

few brief strong storms with downpours and gusty winds each 

afternoon, but overall the severe wx threat will remain low.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 602 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Mainly VFR conditions expected for this TAF cycle. Exceptions

should be CSV/SRB where IFR cigs will be possible again after 07Z

tonight, returned to VFR 13-14Z tomorrow. Isolated showers will

once again be possible Thursday afternoon, but coverage doesn't

warrant prevailing lines. Winds will be light and vrb.



&&



