173

FXUS64 KSHV 062309

AFDSHV



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Shreveport LA

609 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Issued at 1239 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



 - Temperatures are forecasted to increase throughout the

   remainder of the week and into the weekend. 



 - While chances remain low, heat headlines could return as early

   as Thursday and continue into the weekend. 



 - Isolated showers and thunderstorms will be possible across our

   south-central area late into the weekend and early next week. 



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1239 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



The large scale synoptic pattern remains relatively the same and 

mainly features a broad upper-ridge centered around the TX 

panhandle, which is going to keep hot temperatures in our forecast 

due to compressional heating and the upper level winds keeping upper 

level moisture advection at bay. Since moisture will be kept from 

reaching our region, lower humidity will help mitigate the heat 

index from reaching the threshold for heat headlines with average 

heat indices reaching around 97-102 for Wednesday and the lows 

across the region forecasted to fall to the mid 70s. However, as 

the weak progresses the ridge is forecasted to retrograde more 

towards western TX which will cause it's influence over the 

ArkLaTex to weaken into the weekend and early into next week. 



A frontal boundary still is present along the gulf coast which is 

helping prevent surface moisture advection. However, this boundary 

is likely going to erode on Thursday which will cause the chances

of isolated showers and thunderstorms to creep back into the 

forecast for our southernmost region. This erosion will also 

likely cause surface moisture to advect back into our region, 

increasing relative humidity and thus the heat indices. Because 

of this, heat headlines may be issued for Thursday and into the 

weekend as confidence increases.



This pattern will likely remain the same throughout this week, and 

as the upper-level ridge retrogrades, the proceeding upper level 

trough is forecasted to settle over our area, bringing the chance 

for isolated convection across the majority of our Louisiana area. 

Temperatures are forecasted to be relatively the same throughout the 

long term period with highs being in the mid-upper 90s and the lows 

being in the mid and upper 70s. /33/



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 604 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



VFR conditions expected across the airspace at most terminals

through the overnight period. Afternoon CU field is quickly

dissipating with SKC likely through the overnight and early

tomorrow. Vicinity patchy BR may find a way to impact the southern

and eastern terminals late tonight, so a marginal VSBY reduction

was continued over from the previous TAF package. What does

materialize should burn off through mid morning with a period of

SKC before the return of a SCT CU field around 18z. Heights of

the field look to be routine, around 5kft. Terminal winds will

vary through the overnight, with periods of calm conditions

through the morning. That being said, most should carry a S/SW

heading tomorrow afternoon, averaging around 5kt. 



KNAPP



&&



.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...

Issued at 1201 AM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Spotter activation should not be needed for days to come. 



&&



