FIRE WEATHER PLANNING FORECAST FOR SOUTHWEST ALASKA

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE ANCHORAGE AK

313 PM AKDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.DISCUSSION...



A front over Southwest coast this afternoon, bringing wetting 

rains and increasings southeasterly winds to the Bristol Bay 

region and parts of the Kuskokwim Delta. The Lower Kuskokwim 

Valley and interior parts of the Kuskokwim Delta remain warmer and

drier for the remainder of this evening before the front spreads 

rain north across the entirety of mainland Southwest Alaska 

tonight. Rain begins to taper off on Thursday, becoming showery, 

while winds gradually diminish. Rain expected to return to the 

interior Kuskokwim Delta and Lower Kuskokwim Valley by Friday 

night. 



