FNAK53 PAFG 062318

FWFAFG



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Interior Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

318 PM AKDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...RED FLAG WARNING IN EFFECT FOR FIRE WEATHER ZONE 937...



.DISCUSSION...

Thunderstorm potential will be limited to the Eastern Yukon Flats

and AlCan Border this evening. Today and Thursday will be the 

warmest and driest days with temperatures in the 70s across 

Interior Valleys. Min RHs will be dropping with most spots around 

35-45%, but the upper Tanana Valley will drop to 25-30%. Thursday 

will be drier with the southern Yukon Flats and Upper Tanana 

Valley RHs as low as 20-25%. Expect Red Flag Conditions in Isabel 

Pass and Delta Junction Thursday midday into the afternoon as 

winds increase and gust to 50 mph in the pass, and 40 mph in 

Delta. Otherwise, a pattern change hits on Friday with 

temperatures dropping into the 60s. There will be much higher rain

chances, especially in the Northern Interior as a trough then 

dips into Western Alaska this weekend. Looking into next week, it 

looks cooler and wetter overall with little to no significant fire

weather danger.



