.DISCUSSION...



High pressure continues to influence the area keeping temperatures

7 to 10 degrees above average the next several days. 20 foot

winds remain light each day with speeds around 4-7 mph. Dry air

in place will drop min RHs to the 15-25 percent range through the

weekend. Slight chances of rain exist tomorrow afternoon with a

gradual increase in storm chances through the weekend with the best

shot for storms being over the weekend. 



