[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.8158","issue":"2025-08-06T23:24:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS64","cccc":"KBRO","awipsid":"AFDBRO"}]
=================================================



637

FXUS64 KBRO 062324 AAA

AFDBRO



Area Forecast Discussion...UPDATED

National Weather Service Brownsville TX

624 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1213 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



One mid-level ridge of high pressure holds across West Texas and 

the Desert SW into next week while another builds across the 

eastern Gulf, leaving weaker pressure settled in between, along 

the lower Texas coast. Daily pulses of increased moisture continue

low (less than 25 percent) chances for showers and thunderstorms 

along the sea breeze each afternoon, especially Sunday through 

Tuesday. POPs today top off near 20 percent, with guidance 

continuing to trend lower over the past 24 hours. There has been 

no shower activity inland through the morning, with some activity 

across the Gulf waters southwest of the RGV that will continue to 

be monitored. 



Expect near normal temperatures into mid next week, with Heat

Indices of 105 to 110 degrees daily, driving mostly a Moderate

(level 2 of 4) to isolated Major (level 3 of 4) Heat Risk every

day. Special Weather Statements or potentially brief Heat

Advisories may be needed Thursday and Friday. 



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 619 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



VFR conditions will prevail through the cycle. Breezy

southeasterly winds to lessen overnight before picking up again

late Thursday morning. Brief MVFR early this evening remains 

possible with sea breeze showers that pass over a site, although 

chances for this are diminishing rapidly as sunset approaches and 

the boundary pushes northwestward through the region.



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 1213 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Light to moderate southeasterly winds and favorable seas are

expected to prevail through the forecast period. There remains a

low chance of showers and thunderstorms offshore every day into

mid next week.



