Spot Forecast for Upper Williow 2

National Weather Service Missoula MT

526 PM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0700 MDT on August 07. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION...Overcast skies with slight chance of showers

increasing overnight into Thursday morning. Cool temperatures with

showers likely and chance for thunderstorms Thursday afternoon.

Frequent lightning likely with thunderstorm and small hail

possible. 10% chance to get 0.65" or more of precipitation and 

40+ mph outflow winds from direct impact of thunderstorms. Drying

and staying cool with partly cloudy skies into Friday.



.THURSDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Mostly cloudy. Chance of rain showers and

  slight chance of thunderstorms in the morning, then rain showers

  likely and chance of thunderstorms in the afternoon. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...70 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....60 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....63-68. 

* Min Humidity........50-55 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/southwest 1-4 mph with gusts up to

  10 mph in the morning becoming west 5-10 mph with gusts up to 25

  mph in the afternoon. Direct impact from thunderstorm may

  produce erratic gusts 40+ mph. 

* Mixing Height.......Less than 1000 ft agl in the morning

  increasing to near 5500 ft agl in the afternoon. 

* Mixing Winds........West 17 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.11-0.30 inches. 



.THURSDAY NIGHT...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Rain showers likely and

  chance of thunderstorms in the evening, then slight chance of

  rain showers overnight. 

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...90 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....50 percent. 

* Min Temperature.....41-46. 

* Max Humidity........81-86 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........West 5-10 mph with gusts up to 25 mph in the

  evening. Direct impact from thunderstorm may produce erratic

  gusts 40+ mph. Becoming variable/southwest 2-5 mph with gusts 

  up to 18 mph overnight.

* Mixing Height.......Decreasing to near 500 ft agl overnight. 

* Mixing Winds........Southwest 7 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.07-0.35 inches. 



.FRIDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Partly cloudy. Slight chance of rain in the

  morning. Slight chance rain shower or thunderstorm in the

  afternoon.

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...Less than 10 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....Up to 10 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....60-65. 

* Min Humidity........45-50 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/southwest 2-5 mph with gusts up to

  18 mph in the morning becoming west 7-13 mph with gusts up to 30

  mph in the afternoon.

* Mixing Height.......Near 500 ft agl in the morning increasing to

  near 6000 ft agl in the afternoon. 

* Mixing Winds........West 15 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.00-0.02 inches. 



