NZUS99 KABR 062328

WRKKEY



- Patchy fog with visibility averaging around 3 miles expected 

around daybreak Thursday morning, lowest near and south of Watertown.



- An active pattern continues with showers and thunderstorms 

in the forecast through Friday night.



- There is a marginal risk (level 1 out of 5) for severe storms 

south of a line from McIntosh to Watertown this evening if isolated 

storms can form. There is a slight risk (level 2 out of 5) along and 

north of a line from Eagle Butte through Miller to Watertown on 

Thursday. Strong winds and large hail will be the primary threats.



- There is an enhanced risk (level 4 out of 5) for severe weather 

over portions of far northeastern SD into west central MN Friday 

afternoon into Friday night with a slight risk extending westward to 

a line from Eureka to Winner. All hazards are possible including 

tornadoes.



- Hot and humid for Thursday with heat indices as high as 104 over 

portions of central South Dakota.



