Weather Summary for Western and North Central New York

National Weather Service Buffalo NY

730 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



A large area of surface high pressure continues to settle from 

New England to the eastern seaboard through the end of the work

week. A southerly flow on the back side of this surface high 

will allow for a modest increase in moisture that will nudge the

afternoon humidity up, while also allowing for a spot shower or

thunderstorm today, and then east of Lake Ontario on Thursday. 

As surface high pressure remains near our region into the 

weekend, the dry spell is expected to persist through the 

weekend, with modest humidity values early edging higher through

the weekend.



$$



