Grand Junction Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2319 UTC Wednesday, August  6, 2025



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z THURSDAY/...

Issued at 516 PM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025

A few light rain showers will continue to move over the higher

terrain of the southern and central Colorado Divide, but will

taper off over the next 3 or so hours. Skies will clear

overnight, with the gusty southwesterly winds diminishing and

becoming light and terrain driven. These southwesterly winds

will pick up again tomorrow afternoon, with gusts of 20-30 

knots expected. Smoke from regional wildfires will continue to 

produce reduced visibility at certain airports, with KHDN seeing

the greatest impacts.





