Salt Lake City Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2049 UTC Wednesday, August  6, 2025



.AVIATION...KSLC...Westerly winds are expected to continue varying 

between WSW and NW through about 01z as strong valley southwest flow 

interacts with the lake/upvalley northwest flow. Gusts will likely 

prevail around 15-20 knots much of that time, until diminishing 

between 01-02z as an early diurnal shift to SE kicks in around 02-

03z. Clear conditions are expected to persist through the TAF period.

.REST OF UTAH AND SOUTHWEST WYOMING...Gusty southerly/SW winds will 

begin to diminish after 01z. Aside from areas of scattered afternoon 

clouds over the high terrain, mostly clear conditions will persist 

through the TAF period.





