902

FNAK51 PAFC 062330

FWFAER



FIRE WEATHER PLANNING FORECAST FOR SOUTHCENTRAL ALASKA

NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE ANCHORAGE AK

330 PM AKDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.DISCUSSION...



An upper-level ridge promoting the warm and dry weather over 

Southcentral today remains in place through this afternoon before 

sliding east tonight. A building surface ridge out ahead of a 

frontal system in the southwestern Gulf is allowing for the 

development of southerly gap winds this afternoon and through this

evening. Hot, dry, windy conditions are expected to persist 

through this evening in the Copper River Valley as temperatures 

reach the upper 70s, min RH values fall below 25 percent, and 

southerly winds range between 10 to 20 mph with gusts up to 30 

mph. 



The frontal system moves to the northern Gulf Thursday with 

widespread wetting rains for coastal locations and periods of 

light rain for interior valleys. Gusty winds will return for the 

Copper River Valley on Thursday; however, temperatures will be 

cooler with increased cloud cover and scattered showers. 







