=================================================



926

FXUS63 KLBF 062332

AFDLBF



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service North Platte NE

632 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Isolated thunderstorms may be possible this evening and

  Thursday late afternoon/evening



- Heat Advisory in effect from 1pm to 8pm CT Thursday 



- Hot temperatures continue for Friday, along with elevated fire

  weather concerns



- Cooler temperatures this weekend



&&



.SHORT TERM /THROUGH THURSDAY NIGHT/...

Issued at 415 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Kept slight Pops in across the forecast area, however 

confidence is very low. If any storms occur it will be in the 

evening across far northern Nebraska near the NE/SD border, with any 

development from SD that may move southward. Stratus across much of 

the forecast area, generally south of HWY 20 has kept temperatures 

cooler with highs only in the upper 70s to low 80s and the 

environment stable.



Attention then turns to very hot temperatures as an upper level 

ridge moves over the Central Plains. The combinations of air 

temperatures in the 90s to 100s, with strong southerly flow pushing 

dew points in the 70s, RH values reaching 80% by afternoon and heat 

indices above 100 has lead to the issuance of a heat advisory for 

Thursday afternoon. This will generally be for areas along and 

east of HWY 83. There is a marginal risk (level 1 out of 5) for 

portions of the northwest and northern Sandhills on Thursday. 

Thunderstorm development will likely be isolated an mainly 

terrain driven.



&&



.LONG TERM /FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...

Issued at 415 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Another hot day is expected for Friday across most of the 

area, with the exception of the northwest Sandhills, highs will 

reach the upper 90s to low 100s and may need to have heat headlines 

on Friday as well. There will also be an elevated fire weather 

concern on Friday with a ridge breakdown and front passage. Min RH 

will range from 15 to 25 percent across western and southwest 

Nebraska and winds will be around around 15 to 20 mph out of the 

northwest in the afternoon. Frontal passage on Friday will bring 

cooler temperatures in for the weekend into with highs in the 80s. 

Cooler temperatures linger into early next week.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 631 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



LIFR ceilings and visibilities are expected to begin developing

after 09Z across the Sandhills and last through 14Z. This is 

expected at KLBF from 11Z-14Z. Although not included with this 

TAF issuance, this could also develop further north at KVTN. 

Ceilings and visibilities will quickly improve after 14Z, with 

VFR conditions by 15Z. Winds will remain light below 10KT, 

except up to 15KT at KVTN after 17Z. 



&&



.LBF WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

Heat Advisory from 1 PM CDT /noon MDT/ to 8 PM CDT /7 PM MDT/ 

Thursday for NEZ005>010-025>029-036>038-057>059-069>071.



&&



$$



SHORT TERM...Gomez

LONG TERM...Gomez

AVIATION...Roberg



