978

FXUS64 KCRP 062334

AFDCRP



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Corpus Christi TX

634 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Updated at 633 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



- Low 10-20% chance of showers and thunderstorms each day. Higher 

chances across the Coastal Waters.



- Generally minor to moderate risk of heat related impacts across 

South Texas, with a major risk across the northern Brush Country, 

through Saturday. 



- Elevated fire weather conditions across the western Brush

  Country and Rio Grande Plains through the weekend.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 1226 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



A strong mid level high pressure system is currently centered over W 

TX and NM. Drier mid level air will move across S TX tonight on the 

eastern periphery of the high pressure. This will keep rain chances 

less than 20 percent most days through early next week. A few 

streamer showers can be expected along the coast each morning, then 

shifting inland each afternoon along the sea breeze. The Victoria 

Crossroads does see an increase to 30 percent on Sunday due to a mid 

level inverted trough moving across the region and advecting 

slightly deeper moisture into the area.  However, most areas will 

remain dry throughout the period.



Temperatures will be near to slightly above normal through the 

weekend and into next week. Heat indices will generally be 100-109 

each afternoon. A few areas could briefly reach around 110 as the 

sea breeze moves inland. However, conditions should remain below 

Heat Advisory levels due to it being localized and of a short 

duration. Generally there is minor to moderate risk of heat related 

impacts each day. A few locations across the Brush Country may see a 

brief major risk through Friday.



Minimum RH values are expected to be 20-30 percent across the 

western Brush Country and the Rio Grande Plains through the weekend. 

This may lead to elevated fire weather conditions, mostly across 

western portions of Webb County, if winds are slightly higher than 

anticipated. However, winds are expected to remain below

thresholds.



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 633 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



VFR conditions will prevail through the forecast with a brief

instance of MVFR/IFR vsby over the inland Coastal Plains,

impacting VCT/ALI between 09-13Z. Winds will remain generally

light with southeasterly wind gusts around 20 knots in wake of the

afternoon seabreeze. 



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 1226 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



A gentle to at times moderate (BF 3-4) south to southeast flow is

expected to continue through this weekend. There is a low to 

medium chance (10-40%) for showers and thunderstorms through the 

weekend.



&&



