FXUS63 KGRR 062336

AFDGRR



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Grand Rapids MI

736 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Pop-Up Showers and Storms Today and Tomorrow



- Becoming Hot and Humid with Additional Rain Chance Next Week



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 255 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



- Pop-Up Showers and Storms Today and Tomorrow



An axis of 500 J/kg of MLCAPE and higher precipitable water 

values around 1.4 inches is present along and east of the US 127 

corridor. It is in this area that we are seeing isolated showers 

and thunderstorms develop. Winds at the surface and aloft are 

light resulting in little to no movement of these showers and 

storms therefore they will likely collapse on themselves and may 

produce a outflow boundaries where additional showers and storms 

may develop. As we head toward sunset we'll gradually lose our 

instability with shower and thunderstorm chances coming to an end.



Thursday will be quite similar to today although there will be a

shortwave trough moving through with some positive vorticity

advection with additional chances (20 to 30 percent) for showers 

and thunderstorms during the afternoon. Winds toward the surface

and mid levels will again be on the lighter side, expect any

shower or storm that develops to be slow moving. Another shortwave

trough and associated positive vorticity advection ride the ridge

Thursday night which may spark off another round of showers and

thunderstorms with the best chances 40 percent or greater

northwest of Grand Rapids. Dry conditions are then expected for

most of the day Friday.



- Becoming Hot and Humid with Additional Rain Chance Next Week



Dew points increase into the upper 60s to low 70s by Friday and

continue through the weekend. With highs in the mid 80s to mid 90s

heat indices will mainly be in the 90s with values Saturday 

approaching 100. These conditions won't last long though as a 

deeper mid level trough moves through the region for the first 

half of next week. This system will bring with it chances for rain

and storms along with cooler air with highs dropping back into 

the low to mid 80s.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 736 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Earlier thunderstorms and remaining showers near LAN and JXN will

tend to dissipate as the sun goes down. Left behind is cool and 

moist air at the ground, plus VFR cloud decks between 5,000 and 

10,000 ft which should slowly evaporate. This sets up another 

night of IFR mist/fog potential for LAN and JXN, possibly BTL

vicinity too. Some clouds above 15,000 ft moving in tonight could

reduce the fog potential, but that is not a sure bet.



Expecting mostly VFR after 13 Z Thursday with light south-

southwest winds. There is another 20 to 30 percent chance of

showers in the afternoon.



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 255 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



A light breeze over the lake today and Thursday, varying in 

direction with the daytime lake breeze and nighttime land breeze 

circulations. Scattered thunderstorms may be present over Lake 

Michigan Thursday night to early Friday morning according to some 

short-term models, aided by better flow of moist air above the 

marine layer via southwest winds. Friday through the weekend, south-

southeast winds 10-20 knots may build 2 to 4 foot waves and moderate 

swim risk for beaches north of Grand Haven.



&&



.GRR WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

MI...None.

MARINE...None.



&&



$$



DISCUSSION...RAH

AVIATION...CAS

MARINE...RAH



