Service.



.DISCUSSION...

Skies will be mostly clear tonight with temperatures falling from

around 80 degrees at 6 PM, to the lower to mid 60s by Thursday

morning. There's a very small chance for an isolated storm over 

the Black Hills this evening, but it looks like a majority of the 

storms will remain north of the fire area. Winds will continue to 

be light out of the east this evening, with winds becoming more 

westerly on Thursday. Hot and dry conditions are expected on 

Thursday, with RH's dropping down to around 15 percent in the 

afternoon.



