[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.8562","issue":"2025-08-06T23:40:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS63","cccc":"KIWX","awipsid":"AFDIWX"}]
=================================================



045

FXUS63 KIWX 062340

AFDIWX



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Northern Indiana

740 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.KEY MESSAGES...



- Isolated showers across south central Lower Michigan and

  northwest Ohio will continue to diminish this evening.



- Increasingly warmer and more humid conditions are expected

  into the weekend with highs near 90 and heat indices into the

  mid 90s.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 214 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Although upper level heights will slowly increase over the next 

couple of days, there is some smaller chances for showers and storms 

that may exist until it firmly takes hold by Saturday into early 

next week. The initial challenge is with an expanding cu field 

developing due to steep low level lapse rates and over 1000 J/KG of 

SBCAPE. A weak upper wave is working across the area with widely 

scattered showers and storms already developing from Defiance to

Muncie. These should continue to expand north with time and 

eventually dissipate after sunset. If you are fortunate enough 

to see one, heavy rain will be the main concern. 



As the trough axis finally moves east, overall precip chances should 

diminish across the area. MCS development will occur upstream the 

next couple of days with each system working east and possibly SE. 

As is typical, models struggle on overall track and longevity of 

these features with the greatest likihood being their eventual 

demise before reaching the area as they outrun any limited upper 

support and LLJ. Token slight chc pops have been in the forecast

late Thu night into Fri across the far N and NW, but suspect

these will be eliminated with time. 



Friday night into at least Sunday appear to be fairly clear cut with 

no chances for rainfall and afternoon highs into the upper 80s and 

possibly near 90. This combined with dewpoints in the mid 60s to 

locally near 70 will yield heat indices in the 90s. 



All indications are the upper level ridge will begin to flatten next 

week, which will result in at least some confidence on 1 or more 

periods of showers and storms associated with weak disturbances 

rotating through the base of the upper level trough edging into the 

area. Lots of finer details to sort out wrt timing and potential 

hydro/severe concerns that can't be resolved this far out. As a 

result, broadbrushed slight chc to chc pops will continue,



&&



.AVIATION /00Z TAFS THROUGH 00Z FRIDAY/...

Issued at 730 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



An upper level short wave tracking across southern Lower

Michigan into central Indiana combined with a moderate

instability axis across northeast Indiana to produce scattered

showers and isolated thunderstorms this afternoon into early

this evening. Earlier outflow boundary emanating from this

convection north of KFWA appears to have stabilized conditions

with no additional showers expected at the terminal. The main

question for the remainder of the night is on fog potential.

Highest crossover temps appear to be roughly along and southeast

of a Logansport to Fort Wayne to Defiance line. Good radiational

cooling conditions and favorable vertical moisture profiles 

should support at least some patchy fog across the area, with 

potential preference to areas which received rainfall this 

afternoon and where outflow boundaries have modified near sfc 

temp/dewpoint profiles. Did give some consideration to TEMPO IFR

vsbys in fog at KFWA, but will maintain MVFR conditions in 

previous TAF with confidence not quite high enough at this 

point. 



Mainly dry conditions are expected for Thursday, although cannot

completely rule out an isolated shower or storm across NW

Indiana late this period in proximity of better low level

theta-e boundary and where steeper mid level lapse rates are

expected. Weak flow will continue though this forecast valid

period.



&&



.IWX WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

IN...None.

OH...None.

MI...None.

MARINE...None.



&&



$$



DISCUSSION...Fisher

AVIATION...Marsili



