Spot Forecast for Island creek fire

National Weather Service Missoula MT

541 PM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1700 MDT on August 06. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



.DISCUSSION... Mostly cloudy and cool Thursday with chances for 

rain showers in the morning becoming chances for thunderstorms 

with potential for frequent lightning and small hail in the 

afternoon and evening. Chance for wetting rain likely directly 

under thunderstorm. Erratic outflow from direct impact of 

thunderstorm up to 35 mph possible. 10% chance to get 0.55" or

more of precipitation from heavy thundershowers.



.THURSDAY...



* Sky/Weather.........Mostly cloudy. Slight chance rain showers in

  the morning. Chance of thunderstorms and rain showers in the

  afternoon.

* CWR (> 0.10 Inch)...60 percent. 

* Chance Lightning....70 percent. 

* Max Temperature.....65-70. 

* Min Humidity........59-64 percent. 

* Wind (20 ft)........Variable/southwest 1-5 mph with gusts up to

  10 mph in the morning becoming west 5-10 mph with gusts up to 25

  mph in the afternoon. direct impact from thunderstorm may

  produce erratic outflow gust up to 35 mph.

* Mixing Height.......Near 1000 ft agl in the morning increasing

  to near 4000 ft agl in the afternoon.

* Mixing Winds........West-northwest 13 mph. 

* Precip Amount.......0.03-0.26 inches. 



