=================================================



080

FXUS61 KALY 062342

AFDALY



AREA FORECAST DISCUSSION

National Weather Service Albany NY

742 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.SYNOPSIS...

One more day of scattered afternoon and evening showers and 

thunderstorms is forecast on Thursday. Precip chances diminish 

Friday into the weekend, with warming temperatures and humidity 

returning to the region as well.



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Key Messages: 



- There will be a medium chance (30%-60%) of scattered showers 

  and storms again Thursday afternoon.



- Dry conditions, warming temperatures and increasing humidity

  from Friday into early next week.



Scattered showers and thunderstorms are expected to continue

into the evening hours before diminishing due to the loss of

daytime heating. There will once again be a medium chance

(30%-60%) of scattered showers and thunderstorms Thursday 

afternoon, with the highest chances for precipitation across the

higher terrain of the Adirondacks, Berkshires, and Catskills. 

Temperatures will remain warm with highs in the mid to upper 

70s in terrain and into the low to mid 80s in the valleys. Lows 

tonight will fall into the 50s across the terrain, and low to 

mid 60s in the valleys. 



Ensemble guidance remains in good agreement that a ridge at 500

hPa currently located over the Central US will begin building 

east with the ridge axis centered over the East Coast early next

week. This ridge will contribute to warming 850 hPa temperatures

with ensemble mean forecasts ranging between 18-20C by Monday

and Tuesday of next week. Daily high temperatures are forecast

to rise through the weekend with into early next week with highs

reaching the mid 80s to lower 90s by Monday and Tuesday. Humidity

values will also be on the increase early next week with 

northward moisture advection strengthening. While this will 

result in feels like temperatures climbing above 90 in the 

valley locations, the likelihood of multiple hours above 95 

degree, and the need for Heat Advisories, currently looks to be

less than 25% on both Monday and Tuesday.



The next chance for active weather looks to be next Wednesday 

with a 500 hPa trough forecast to potentially approach the 

region. However, there is both amplitude and phase uncertainty 

in the evolution of the trough, with two main scenarios emerging

from the ensemble guidance. The first scenario (consisting of

roughly 55% of ensemble members) has a less amplified and more 

progressive trough which would bring a medium chance for showers

and thunderstorms to most of the region Wednesday afternoon. 

The second scenario (consisting of 45% of ensemble members) has 

a deeper and slower trough which would result in increased

chances for rainfall being closer to Wednesday evening/night and

greater rainfall totals (with a medium chance for 24 hour totals

greater than 0.25"). Regardless of the scenario, temperatures 

look to be slightly cooler with higher returning to the mid-to- 

upper 80s.



&&



.AVIATION /00Z THURSDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...

Lingering evening showers at KPSF through 01Z/Thu, with

additional showers/thunderstorms north of KGFL which should

weaken but could produce some showers between 01Z-03Z/Thu.

Otherwise, some fog is likely to develop in the wake of today's

rain at KPSF, with a period of MVFR/IFR conditions expected

overnight. Elsewhere, mainly VFR conditions are expected outside

any showers and late night fog at KGFL. VFR conditions Thursday,

although can not rule out a few reductions to MVFR due to

lingering haze/smoke.



Light/variable winds overnight will trend into the southeast to

south at 5-10 KT Thursday afternoon.



Outlook...



Thursday Night: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Friday: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Friday Night: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Saturday: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Saturday Night: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Sunday: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Sunday Night: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.

Monday: No Operational Impact. NO SIG WX.



&&



.ALY WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

CT...None.

NY...Air Quality Alert until midnight EDT tonight for NYZ038>041-

     043-047>054-058>061-063>066-082-084.

MA...Air Quality Alert until midnight EDT tonight for MAZ001-025.

VT...Air Quality Alert until midnight EDT tonight for VTZ013>015.



&&



$$



