244

FXUS64 KJAN 062343

AFDJAN



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Jackson MS

643 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 203 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Through The Next Week...



The ridge axis and attendant 'heat dome' will continue to drift 

eastward from upstream. This will have the effect of raising our 

heat indices, west of I-55 back into the mid triple digits by early 

next week. As such we may be looking to issue heat-related 

hazards/products for those areas come next week. 



Elsewhere there remains a chance for scattered afternoon/evening 

showers, and embedded thunderstorms along our eastern most corridor, 

extending through to south-south eastern portions of the CWA. There 

is still some disagreement about the overall lower level pattern 

which has caused a bit of hesitance about issuing more deterministic 

products regarding both TS coverage and heat index values./OAJ/



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 641 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



All TAF sites are VFR this afternoon and this will continue

through this evening, with the exception of some possible

continued shower/thunderstorm activity at HBG/PIB until 01-02Z. 

Some stratus/fog development is possible early Thursday morning, 

which may bring MVFR conditions to HBG/PIB. /15/



&&



