Recreation Forecast

National Weather Service Grand Forks ND

648 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Here are the Recreation Area Forecasts...



Wave height forecasts represent the average of the highest 33% of

waves that occur in a given period. Since the significant wave

height is an average of the largest waves, mariners should be

aware that many individual waves will be higher. 



For Devils Lake...



.TONIGHT...Southwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Mostly clear. Lows in the mid 60s. 

.THURSDAY...Southeast winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Mostly sunny. Highs in the 80s. 

.THURSDAY NIGHT...Southeast winds 10 to 20 mph. Waves 1 foot or

less. Scattered thunderstorms through the night. Showers in the

late evening and overnight. Mostly cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 





For the Upper and Lower Red Lakes...



.TONIGHT...Southwest winds around 10 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Partly cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 

.THURSDAY...Southwest winds around 10 mph in the morning becoming

light. Waves 1 foot or less. Sunny. Highs 75 to 85. 

.THURSDAY NIGHT...Light winds becoming southeast 10 to 15 mph in

the late evening and overnight. Waves 1 foot or less. Partly

cloudy in the evening then becoming mostly cloudy. Lows in the

upper 60s. 





For Lake of the Woods...



.TONIGHT...Southwest winds 10 to 15 mph. Waves 1 foot or less.

Scattered thunderstorms in the evening. Isolated showers in the

late evening and overnight. Patchy fog after midnight. Partly

cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 

.THURSDAY...Southwest winds around 10 mph until late afternoon

becoming light. Waves 1 foot or less. Sunny. Highs in the 70s. 

.THURSDAY NIGHT...Light winds becoming southeast around 10 mph

after midnight. Waves 1 foot or less. Partly cloudy in the

evening then becoming mostly cloudy. Lows in the mid 60s. 





