[{"xmlns":"nwws-oi","id":"nwws_processor.8931","issue":"2025-08-06T23:51:00Z","ttaaii":"FXUS64","cccc":"KAMA","awipsid":"AFDAMA"}]
=================================================



417

FXUS64 KAMA 062351

AFDAMA



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Amarillo TX

651 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.KEY MESSAGES...

Issued at 1224 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



- Hot temperatures around or just over 100 degrees are forecast

  for the next few days.



- Daily thunderstorm chances return this weekend through early

  next week along with temperatures closer to average.



&&



.SHORT TERM...

(This evening through Thursday night)

Issued at 133 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



High pressure remains in place across much of the southern and

southwestern CONUS for today and tomorrow. With high pressure in

place over the Panhandles, this will allow temperatures to warm up

with widespread highs in the upper 90s to just over 100 degrees

for this afternoon. The hotter temperatures are due in part to 

much drier conditions at the surface with southwest downslope 

winds. Dry conditions are expected for the rest of the day with a 

very low chance (less than 10 percent) for a shower or storm to 

reach the northwestern Panhandles from convection that is 

currently starting over the higher terrain of New Mexico.



High temperatures tomorrow will once again be above average on

Thursday with current forecast highs in the upper 90s to just over

100 degrees. West to southwest downslope winds will continue to

usher in dry air tomorrow so temperatures may be able to warm up a

degree or two more than today. The main limiting factor to the

temperatures for tomorrow will be afternoon cumulus development 

across the area. Sufficient heating will allow temperatures to 

approach convective temperature values and with mid level moisture

remaining in place, isolated showers or storms may form during 

the afternoon into the early evening hours. Some model guidance 

even has a weak disturbance rounding the high pressure system 

tomorrow afternoon/evening which may aid in developing some 

isolated showers or storms. There is not a lot of instability as 

depicted by forecast soundings and there is a lot of dry air in 

the lower levels so there is much uncertainty on how much rain may

actually be able to reach the surface. Even if most of the 

showers remain as virga, strong downburst wind gusts (potentially 

even localized severe wind gusts) will be possible given DCAPE 

values around or over 2000 J/kg.



Muscha



&&



.LONG TERM...

(Friday through next Tuesday)

Issued at 133 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



H500 high pressure looks to remain in place over the region on

Friday. High temperatures may still remain at or just above the

100 degree mark on Friday afternoon. Temperatures beyond Friday

should slowly decrease down to near average for the rest of the

long term forecast as high pressure moves off to the west and

surface moisture increases. The finer details of the upper level

pattern next week remain uncertain as model guidance diverges on

the specifics, but in general an active pattern with daily chances

for thunderstorms looks to return starting this weekend. Model

soundings even indicate that a return of strong to severe storms

may be possible during this time frame as well with ample

instability in place over the region.



Muscha



&&



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Issued at 649 PM CDT Wed Aug 6 2025



VFR conditions over the next 24 hours at all TAF sites with winds

out of the south to southwest in the 10-15kt range gusts up to

25kts at times. Mostly clear skies to few high clouds. Very low

chance <5% of a pop up storm at KDHT this evening. 



Weber



&&



.AMA WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

TX...Heat Advisory until 9 PM CDT this evening for TXZ001>003-006>008-

     011>013-016>018-317.



     Heat Advisory from 1 PM to 8 PM CDT Thursday for TXZ317.



OK...Heat Advisory until 9 PM CDT this evening for OKZ001-002.



&&



$$



SHORT TERM...05

LONG TERM....05

AVIATION...89



