.NOW...

Through 900 PM, showers and thunderstorms will to move southwest at 

near 10 knots along the waters of the Outer Gulf, bayside, and 

gulfside waters. Some showers are developing over the Florida Straits

near Floyd's Wall. The heaviest activity is located north of Big Pine

Key. Mariners encountering the heaviest activity may experience 

gusty and erratic winds of 25 to 30 knots, reduced visibility in 

moderate to heavy downpours, and isolated lightning strikes.



