FNAK52 PAFG 070002

FWFWCZ



Fire Weather Planning Forecast for Western Alaska

National Weather Service Fairbanks AK

402 PM AKDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.DISCUSSION...

Warmer and drier weather today as ridging settles in over the

region. These conditions continue through tomorrow morning before

the pattern shifts due to a low in the Bering Sea moving east 

into the Gulf of Alaska. As the low progresses eastward, showers 

return to the Lower Yukon and YK Deltas, then spread north into 

the western Interior and eastern Seward Peninsula Thursday night 

into Friday. These showers are expected to bring high temperatures

down into the mid to low 60s, with min RH values increasing

into the 70% range. Isolated thunderstorms are possible with these

showers, but will mainly effect the western Interior and eastern

Seward Peninsula. Wetting rains are highly likely to be

associated with these storms through the weekend. Winds are

expected to remain fairly light and out of th northeast through

Thursday morning, but shifts towards the south/southwest by

Thursday night. Looking ahead, broad scale troughing continues

keeping conditions cool and moist going into next week. 



