CWFJAX



Coastal Waters Forecast for Northeast Florida/Southeast Georgia

National Weather Service Jacksonville FL

808 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Atlantic Coastal Waters from Altamaha Sound GA to Flagler Beach

FL out to 60 nm.



Seas are provided as a range of the average height of the highest

1/3 of the waves, along with the occasional height of the average

highest 1/10 of the waves.



AMZ400-071515-

Synopsis for Altamaha Sound GA to Flagler Beach FL out to 60 nm-

808 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



.SYNOPSIS...



A frontal boundary will remain over the region through Thursday. This

front will then drift south across central Florida Friday through

the early part of next week. This boundary will result in unsettled

weather throughout this period, with daily rounds of showers and 

thunderstorms.



The National Hurricane Center is monitoring an area that may become 

a tropical cyclone near the Southeastern U.S. coast late this week

into this weekend. Continue to monitor NHC forecasts through the 

week.



.GULF STREAM...



The approximate location of the west wall of the Gulf Stream as of

Aug 05, 2025 at 1200 UTC...



 36 nautical miles east of Flagler Beach.

 56 nautical miles east southeast of Saint Augustine Beach.

 82 nautical miles east southeast of Jacksonville Beach.

 94 nautical miles east of St Simons Island.



This data courtesy of the Naval Oceanographic Office.



