=================================================



782

FXUS62 KTBW 070008

AFDTBW



Area Forecast Discussion

National Weather Service Tampa Bay Ruskin FL

808 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



...New AVIATION...



.AVIATION...

(00Z TAFS)

Lingering and weakening ISOLD TSRAs remain around the terminals

this evening with very limited and brief flight restrictions and 

will keep VCTS thru 01Z-02Z. Overnight winds become light NE with 

clearing skies for VFR conditions through Thu morning before 

another active afternoon of +TSRAs aft 17-18Z Thu. 



&&



.DISCUSSION...

Issued at 245 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



We are gradually transitioning from our south-southwest flow to an 

easterly flow regime by tomorrow. This afternoon we will see some 

sea breeze showers and thunderstorms populate the coast and 

eventually make their way inland. However, there is not a lot of 

strong-steering wind today and the chances for localized flooding 

are heightened. Tonight, the easterly low-level flow strengthens 

and increased rain chances are expected for southwestern FL which 

will move into the Gulf overnight.



Tomorrow, as that weak area of low pressure still sits on the 

southeastern U.S. coast, plentiful moisture (PWAT of 2.0-2.4) will 

support scattered to widespread afternoon and evening convection. 

NHC still has that area flagged with a 40% chance of development 

in the next 7 days.



Late this week and into the weekend, atmospheric moisture persists 

under the weak inverted trough and scattered to numerous showers 

and storms continue each afternoon and evening. Temperatures cool 

slightly into the upper 80s/lower 90s with this increased moisture 

and cloud coverage.



By early to mid next week we start to transition back into our 

typical summertime southeast flow pattern with afternoon

convection. 



&&



.MARINE...

Issued at 245 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



High pressure will remain over the waters with light winds around

10 knots or less and slight seas. Shower and thunderstorm chances

will gradually rise through the week as moisture increases over 

the area.



&&



.FIRE WEATHER...

Issued at 245 PM EDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Abundant moisture will keep RH values above critical levels through

the week. Scattered to numerous showers and thunderstorms are

expected each day. Outside of thunderstorms, winds will remain 

light at 10 mph or less, precluding any fire weather concerns.



&&



.PRELIMINARY POINT TEMPS/POPS...

TPA  80  94  79  92 /  30  70  70  90 

FMY  77  94  77  92 /  50  80  50  90 

GIF  76  95  77  93 /  40  70  60  90 

SRQ  77  94  76  92 /  40  60  70  90 

BKV  74  94  73  92 /  30  70  60  90 

SPG  80  91  78  90 /  30  60  70  90 



&&



Sea Breeze Thunderstorm Regime For Thursday: 2

Sea Breeze Thunderstorm Regime For Friday: 2



For additional information on sea breeze regimes, go to: 

     https://www.weather.gov/tbw/ThunderstormClimatology



&&



.TBW WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...

FL...None.

Gulf waters...None.



&&



$$



