Denver/Boulder Aviation Discussion

Issued at 2053 UTC Wednesday, August  6, 2025



.AVIATION /18Z TAFS through 18Z Thursday/...

Issued at 1131 AM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025

Generally VFR conditions through the TAF period with light winds.

Fairly low confidence in the diurnal wind cycle today, with

guidance split between mixing down some west-northwest winds or a

more typical turn to the northeast. Would expect something in

between, with a gradual clockwise turn through the afternoon

hours. Main concern this afternoon is the potential for some high

based virga/showers with gusty outflow winds. Best chance of

impacts is at APA but can't rule out a wind shift later on at DEN

this afternoon. Drainage is expected to prevail this evening 

through most of the overnight hours, with a gradual turn to the 

west likely Thursday morning.

Smoke is expected to linger across the area through the TAF

period, though the highest concentrations of 1-6km AGL smoke

should remain north of the terminals. There may be occasional

slant range visibility issues, particularly in the early morning 

hours as smoke attempts to settle a little bit... but forecast 

near surface smoke concentrations don't appear to be high enough 

to add in any FU at this time.





