FNUS75 KLKN 070020

FWSLKN



Spot Forecast for Jakes Fire...BLM

National Weather Service Elko NV

520 PM PDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 0600 PDT on August 07. 

If conditions become unrepresentative, contact the National Weather

Service.



Please contact National Weather Service Elko if you have questions

or concerns with this forecast.



.DISCUSSION...

Elevated fire weather condtions are expected from 11 AM PDT

Thursday morning until 10 PM PDT Thursday afternoon due to

southwest to west wind gusts near 25 mph and minimum relative

humidity values as low as 12 percent. Critical fire weather (Red

Flag) condtions will remain east of the fire in Central and

Eastern Elko County. 



.THURSDAY...



Sky/weather.........Mostly sunny (10-20 percent). 

Max temperature.....82-85. 

Min humidity........12-17 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........Northwest 6-8 mph shifting to southwest to 

                    west by late morning. Southwest to west 

                    winds increasing to 15-20 mph in the 

                    afternoon. Frequent wind gusts near 25 mph 

                    in the afternoon. 

 Slope/valley.......Northwest 7-9 mph shifting to southwest to 

                    west by late morning. Southwest to west 

                    winds increasing to 15-20 mph in the 

                    afternoon. Frequent wind gusts near 25 mph 

                    in the afternoon. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......Increasing to around 9100 ft AGL in the 

                    afternoon. 

Transport winds.....West 19-21 mph. 



.THURSDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Partly cloudy (40-50 percent). Areas of smoke 

                    in the evening. 

Min temperature.....55-58. 

Max humidity........32-37 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........Southwest to west 15-20 mph in the evening 

                    shifting to north and decreasing to 11-13 mph 

                    overnight. Wind gusts near 25 mph in the 

                    evening.   

 Slope/valley.......Southwest to west winds 15-20 mph in the 

                    evening shifting to north and decreasing to 

                    12-14 mph overnight. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......Lowering to 500 ft AGL or less. 

Transport winds.....North 19-21 mph. 



.FRIDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny (0-10 percent). 

Max temperature.....79-82. 

Min humidity........10-15 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........North 5-7 mph in the morning shifting to 

                    northwest and increasing to 7-9 mph in 

                    the afternoon. 

 Slope/valley.......North winds 6-8 mph in the morning shifting 

                    to northwest and increasing to 8-10 mph in 

                    the afternoon.  

CWR.................0 percent. 

Mixing height.......Increasing to around 9200 ft AGL in the 

                    afternoon. 

Transport winds.....Northwest 9-11 mph. 



$$



