FWSBYZ



Spot Forecast for JK Butte...BLM

National Weather Service Billings MT

629 PM MDT Wed Aug 6 2025



Forecast is based on forecast start time of 1800 MDT on August 06. 

If conditions become unrepresentative...contact the National Weather

Service.



Please contact our office if you have questions or concerns with 

this forecast.



.DISCUSSION...

Expect thunderstorm activity to stay south of the fire location 

this evening, but cannot completely rule out a stray thunderstorm 

closer to the fire between now and 9pm (10% chance). Winds on the 

ridgetop will increase out of the southeast with gusts up to 35 

mph after sunset. Highest gusts are expected between 9pm-4am. No 

thunderstorms are expected late tonight and Thursday, but there is

a risk of storms (possibly severe w/ hail, strong wind gusts and 

heavy rain) along a cold front Thursday night into Friday. 



.TONIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Partly cloudy with isolated nearby thunderstorms 

                    until 9pm. Erratic wind gusts to 40 mph possible

                    near storms.

CWR.................Less than 5 percent. 

Chance of lightning.10 percent. 

Min temperature.....63-67. 

Max humidity........78-82 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......Southeast 10-20 mph. 

 Ridgetop...........Southeast 15-25 mph. Gusts to 35 mph after

                    sunset. 

Mixing height.......Decreasing to 800 ft AGL overnight. 

Transport winds.....Southeast 22 mph. 



.THURSDAY...



Sky/weather.........Sunny. 

CWR.................0 percent. 

Chance of lightning.0 percent. 

Max temperature.....91-95. 

Min humidity........25-29 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......Southeast to south 6-12 mph shifting to the 

                    west by noon, then northwest 12-18 mph in 

                    the afternoon. 

 Ridgetop...........South 10-20 mph early, becoming west to 

                    northwest in the afternoon.

Mixing height.......Increasing to 5500 ft AGL in the afternoon. 

Transport winds.....South 12 mph shifting to the west-northwest

                    at 15 mph.



.THURSDAY NIGHT...



Sky/weather.........Mostly cloudy. Slight chance of thunderstorms 

                    after 9pm, then chance of thunderstorms 

                    overnight. Erratic wind gusts to 50+ mph 

                    possible near storms.

CWR.................25 percent. 

Chance of lightning.30 percent. 

Min temperature.....62-66. 

Max humidity........82-87 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......North 5-15 mph.

 Ridgetop...........North to northeast 10-20 mph. 

Mixing height.......Decreasing to 500 ft AGL overnight. 

Transport winds.....North 13 mph. 



.FRIDAY...



Sky/weather.........Partly sunny. Slight chance of showers and 

                    thunderstorms in the morning, then chance of 

                    showers and thunderstorms in the afternoon. 

CWR.................15 percent. 

Chance of lightning.30 percent. 

Max temperature.....76-80. 

Min humidity........37-41 percent. 

Wind (20 ft)........ 

 Slope/valley.......Northwest 10-20 mph. Gusts to 25 mph after 10am.

 Ridgetop...........Northwest 15-25 mph gusting to 30 mph. 

Mixing height.......Increasing to 6000 ft AGL in the afternoon. 

Transport winds.....Northwest 20 mph. 



